Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.16,0:00:19.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roy Mustang observation journal...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.66,0:00:20.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.57,0:00:25.17,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,As it turns out, I've been ordered by \NInternal Affairs to inspect my superior officer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.92,0:00:29.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"In order that we may understand how your days are spent,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.58,0:00:34.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,those who are most suited to the task \Nare to conduct a top-secret inspection."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.26,0:00:37.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, Lieutenant Havoc, \Nyou're inspecting Colonel Mustang?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.42,0:00:40.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. But I can't investigate him \Nall on my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.92,0:00:42.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want all of you to help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.68,0:00:47.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Saturday, 0946 hours:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.37,0:00:52.15,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Colonel Mustang bluntly calls the documents before him that are due at noon to be a pain."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.69,0:00:54.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Similarly, Saturday, 1026 hours:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.81,0:00:58.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel attempted to feed Lieutenant Hawkeye's dog."
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.41,0:01:00.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Also, 1103 hours:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.36,0:01:03.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Colonel suddenly began to clean the windows."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.06,0:01:05.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Will he be able to \Nmeet his deadline?"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.42,0:01:07.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"1147 hours:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.32,0:01:10.61,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,the Colonel begins signing the documents as \Nhe makes a fuss about not having enough time."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.61,0:01:12.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"But he {\i1}did{\i0} have time."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.83,0:01:16.18,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,"In the afternoon, the Colonel conducted an \Ninspection of the fire-fighting facilities around town."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.18,0:01:19.68,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,"At this time, the Colonel received a letter \Nfrom the woman working at the flower shop."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.32,0:01:22.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"It appears that the letter is an invitation to a date."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.16,0:01:25.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Have witnessed tickets to a play."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.44,0:01:27.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"The Colonel readied to leave,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.59,0:01:30.50,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,saying he was gathering municipal intelligence, and would go directly home afterward."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.50,0:01:32.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Judging by his face, \Nhe is clearly going on a date."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.69,0:01:36.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a minute! The woman at the flower shop! You mean Grace?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.64,0:01:39.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I thought her attitude toward me had cooled off lately. Is that what's going on?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.18,0:01:41.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"What's this, Lieutenant? \NYou were seeing that girl?"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.75,0:01:43.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"You're out of luck \Nagainst the Colonel."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.60,0:01:45.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"I'm sorry to hear that. Please give up on her."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.55,0:01:46.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop making light of it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.48,0:01:49.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"How could you guys \Nknow how I feel?!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.96,0:01:52.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"It's your fault you got dumped. No question about it."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.42,0:01:53.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Shut up, you big dope!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.55,0:01:55.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"No, you are!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.65,0:01:55.66,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,"What did you call me?!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.66,0:01:56.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Attaboy, get him, get him!"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.89,0:01:59.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Don't be so rough on each other. \NLet's all get along."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.47,0:02:00.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I quit! I quit!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.26,0:02:04.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How am I supposed to do this investigation?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.90,0:02:09.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.58,0:02:14.12,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Here at the Central Command Center, \Nthere are brave soldiers who have no trouble
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.12,0:02:16.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,sacrificing whatever it takes in order to achieve peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.49,0:02:22.33,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,These are the tales of love and courage of the Flame Alchemist—Colonel Roy Mustang—and his men.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.96,0:04:03.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yo,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.01,0:04:04.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Black Hayate.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.57,0:04:07.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure must be nice for you,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.91,0:04:10.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,leading a happy-go-lucky life.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.78,0:04:18.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter with \NLieutenant Havoc?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.63,0:04:20.92,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,He must've had his heart broken again or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.12,0:04:20.92,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,That was sharp.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.92,0:04:23.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't get much time off \Nwhen you take on military duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.73,0:04:26.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It must be hard finding a woman who will go out with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.15,0:04:28.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's pathetic.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.41,0:04:31.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If he were a man, he'd find a way to handle both his work and women.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.23,0:04:32.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's your fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.87,0:04:36.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Still, as things are, \Nit's interfering with his duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.68,0:04:39.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, someone introduce a woman to Havoc.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.88,0:04:42.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Please don't ask the impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.41,0:04:43.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want someone to introduce me!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.77,0:04:45.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Colonel, why don't you share one of yours?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.30,0:04:47.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.39,0:04:49.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.46,0:04:52.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does anyone know what \Nkind of woman Havoc likes?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.40,0:04:54.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, the other day, when I was out drinking with Havoc,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.88,0:04:59.40,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,he complained to me, "Aren't there any \Ncheerful, well-adjusted beauties out there?"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.40,0:05:00.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right, Warrant Officer Falman,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.77,0:05:03.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,secure a cheerful, \Nwell-adjusted beauty at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.40,0:05:04.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Introduce her to Lt. Havoc.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.65,0:05:06.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want {\i1}me{\i0} to?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.16,0:05:08.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Remember, you're on a mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.16,0:05:11.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a mission for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.07,0:05:15.62,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,All the materials on Brig. Gen. Basque Grand, \NDoctor Marcoh, and Shou Tucker.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.36,0:05:20.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Also, put together all the records on \Nthe 5th Laboratory and the 2nd Prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.07,0:05:21.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.13,0:05:24.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does that include the items \Nlost in the Central Library fire?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.92,0:05:28.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not ask me the obvious. That is why I called on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.01,0:05:32.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If this can get me into the \NCourt-Martial Office again,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.94,0:05:35.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I might be able to more closely investigate the incident involving Brig. Gen. Hughes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.66,0:05:36.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is your answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.66,0:05:38.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yes! Understood!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.33,0:05:43.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A mission, he says. \NI haven't had any training in flirting.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.23,0:05:44.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the world coming to?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.93,0:05:51.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon! \NAre you all right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.68,0:05:52.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.53,0:05:53.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Warrant Officer Falman!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.76,0:05:56.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Long time no see.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.06,0:05:57.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Have you been \Ngetting along okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.72,0:05:59.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.25,0:06:00.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,more or less.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.27,0:06:03.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.82,0:06:07.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka, I'm looking for a cheerful, well-adjusted beauty right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.49,0:06:08.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you know anyone like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.81,0:06:10.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do I know anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.04,0:06:15.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So what you're insinuating is that I'm {\i1}not{\i0} a cheerful, well-adjusted beauty, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.16,0:06:16.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, it's not like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.38,0:06:21.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Under the Colonel's orders, I have to introduce Lt. Havoc to a new girlfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.47,0:06:22.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Girlfriend?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.19,0:06:24.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you have anyone in mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.73,0:06:26.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, in that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.49,0:06:27.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have a grand idea!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.66,0:06:31.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major Armstrong's sister?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.91,0:06:32.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.97,0:06:36.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He said that she is of marrying age but is so shy that she cannot find a boyfriend.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.27,0:06:51.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Incredible...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.06,0:06:53.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think I'd better go...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.30,0:06:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.18,0:07:01.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If she starts talking about tying the knot, you'll be taking one wealthy wife!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.00,0:07:03.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll be on easy street!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.20,0:07:06.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I haven't even met her yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.27,0:07:10.53,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,From what Major Armstrong says, \Nshe has the same dashing looks that he does.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.53,0:07:12.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Major's sister \Nlooks just like him?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.04,0:07:17.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it, I'm leaving!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.77,0:07:21.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you for coming, Lt. Havoc!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.33,0:07:23.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've been waiting for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.08,0:07:24.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, good luck!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.63,0:07:32.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Over the span of 180 years, the Armstrong family has been involved in enterprises
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.88,0:07:37.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that are deeply tied in with the political and economic affairs of this land.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.44,0:07:41.64,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,For generations, it has been a noble family that has served in the military government
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.64,0:07:45.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and has been a pillar of support \Nto this nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.12,0:07:47.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I myself have served in \Nthe military government...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.65,0:07:51.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Every time I hear Father tell the story, it is marvelous.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.08,0:07:53.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh my, Dear,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.75,0:07:55.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,are you boasting \Nto the guests again?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.73,0:07:57.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Mother...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.16,0:07:58.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.52,0:08:01.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Thank goodness!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.16,0:08:03.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The mother is quite norm—
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.67,0:08:08.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She's huge! \NShe's not at all normal!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.62,0:08:11.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hold on a minute now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.17,0:08:14.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The father is wide and fat,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.68,0:08:17.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and the mother is long and tall.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.75,0:08:21.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Add them together, and their son \Nwould sum up like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.10,0:08:25.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which means, when it \Ncomes to their daughter...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.58,0:08:34.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catch me if you can!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.43,0:08:38.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, both parents' features don't always necessarily get passed down.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.96,0:08:41.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a chance that she leans more toward one side.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.47,0:08:44.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then, Lieutenant, \Nallow me to introduce my sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.46,0:08:47.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come along, Catherine. \NDon't be shy. Come in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.84,0:08:50.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which is she?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.94,0:08:53.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does she take after her father, \Nor her mother?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.30,0:08:55.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I couldn't stand it either way, but between the two of them,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.18,0:08:56.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}at least let her \Ntake after her mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.76,0:08:57.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.23,0:08:59.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.72,0:09:02.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.25,0:09:05.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm Catherine Elle Armstrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.62,0:09:08.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hooray for mutations!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.23,0:09:11.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well? Isn't she beautiful? She looks just like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.32,0:09:11.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which part?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.38,0:09:14.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Her lower eyelashes, and such.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.55,0:09:15.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't say.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.99,0:09:18.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come now, Catherine. \NDon't be shy.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.87,0:09:20.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,R-Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.00,0:09:22.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, Catherine-san, \Nwhat are your hobbies?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.50,0:09:25.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's see... a little piano...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.92,0:09:30.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How cute! There's no way \Nthis girl is the Major's sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.92,0:09:34.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I lift a little piano...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.42,0:09:37.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is the matter, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.93,0:09:41.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I take that back. \NShe absolutely is the Major's sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.48,0:09:45.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But then again, if you take away her monstrous strength, there's...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.14,0:09:46.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}her looks...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.14,0:09:47.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}her figure...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.14,0:09:48.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}her assets...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.15,0:09:49.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and her influence.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.15,0:09:51.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does that make it all okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.21,0:09:52.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is this...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.61,0:09:55.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the prime of my life?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.70,0:09:56.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Catherine-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.43,0:09:57.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.27,0:09:58.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If it's all right with you,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.39,0:10:01.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,would you allow me \Nthe chance to go out with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.99,0:10:08.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Havoc-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.87,0:10:11.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.94,0:10:13.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.36,0:10:15.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.74,0:10:18.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.15,0:10:20.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,prefer men who are \Nmore like my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.47,0:10:28.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Havoc-san, you are not my type, \Nso let's pretend we never spoke of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.51,0:10:30.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.70,0:10:32.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh? What's the matter, Lieutenant?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.61,0:10:34.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,10,000 cens says he blows it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.32,0:10:35.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,10,000 cens says she turns him down.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.95,0:10:38.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, 30,000 cens says \Nthey call the whole thing off.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.75,0:10:40.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That doesn't make for \Nmuch of a wager, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.54,0:10:41.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.42,0:10:45.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did I even come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.84,0:11:00.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, Major Armstrong is exactly the kind of man I figured him for.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.45,0:11:02.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Hawkeye, \Ncan you put out a dragnet?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.90,0:11:03.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.00,0:11:08.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm starving.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.51,0:11:12.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had to go without lunch ever since I lost that bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.18,0:11:14.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won, so I've been \Neating my fill.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.39,0:11:16.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please buy me something!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.11,0:11:19.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If I did that, the bet wouldn't mean anything, would it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.45,0:11:23.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aren't those fixed yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.24,0:11:26.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I sure do hate this. \NThe whole area is creepy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.05,0:11:29.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are even stories of ghosts appearing here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.79,0:11:40.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that sound?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.23,0:11:41.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.58,0:11:48.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.42,0:11:54.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.43,0:11:57.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't do that...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.02,0:12:00.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're tickling me...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.05,0:12:14.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.83,0:12:17.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.20,0:12:19.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sit!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.50,0:12:20.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shake!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.61,0:12:21.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The other one!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.78,0:12:22.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lie down!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.91,0:12:23.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.39,0:12:38.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Good morning, Lieutenant.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.97,0:12:39.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.78,0:12:41.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, seriously?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.90,0:12:43.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, seriously.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.02,0:12:45.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The stories are true!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.12,0:12:48.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give me a break! I won't be able to go out walking at night anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.07,0:12:49.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Has something happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.73,0:12:52.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say they saw the 13th warehouse. What nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.26,0:12:55.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not nonsense, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.16,0:12:57.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right! \NWe really are scared here!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.42,0:12:59.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The 13th warehouse?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.67,0:13:03.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Military warehouses are only supposed to go up to the 12th warehouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.33,0:13:06.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say that there's \Na 13th one that appears!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.60,0:13:11.02,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,In fact, they say that the location where it stands was an execution ground a long time ago!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.02,0:13:13.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When night falls, \Nthe 13th warehouse
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.63,0:13:16.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,appears in the place where \Nthere should only be twelve of them!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.42,0:13:19.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the ghosts of those who were executed there long ago
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.45,0:13:21.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,can be heard scra... scraping,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.78,0:13:25.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,digging up the ground, \Nlooking for their own bodies!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.30,0:13:28.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ha! That's ridiculous. \NYou look at things in a state of fear,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.53,0:13:31.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so you're just imagining the things \Nthat you're afraid of.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.47,0:13:33.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You must've just mistook it \Nfor something else.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.04,0:13:34.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, aren't you afraid?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.86,0:13:37.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Of course not. \NAlchemists are scientists.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.92,0:13:41.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's our job to always look at things \Nwith a logical mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.30,0:13:43.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we're not the \Nonly ones who saw it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.93,0:13:45.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are stories all over the Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.80,0:13:48.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is pathetic. \NYou call yourselves soldiers?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.70,0:13:51.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm going to reveal the reality of the situation
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.21,0:13:53.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to those who would spread these kinds of stories!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.02,0:13:54.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.65,0:13:58.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Everyone, rejoice! The Colonel says \Nhe's going to join our operation tonight!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.10,0:14:00.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's our colonel! \NHe thinks about his men!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.42,0:14:03.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank goodness! With the Colonel along, there's nothing to be afraid of!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.79,0:14:05.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a minute! \NWhat are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.40,0:14:08.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know, tonight's operation to uncover the truth about the ghostly phenomena.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.60,0:14:11.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going to show us \Nthe reality of it, right, Colonel?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.05,0:14:12.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I did say that, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.80,0:14:15.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid to go home to the dorms at night.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.49,0:14:17.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please help us, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.86,0:14:26.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For crying out loud, why do I have to \Ntag along on their little test of courage?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.99,0:14:29.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They all adore you, Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.09,0:14:32.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why should I be pleased \Nover being adored by men?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.18,0:14:34.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How can men serve as soldiers against flesh-and-blood men,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.35,0:14:37.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,when something they can't even see makes them jump out of their skin?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.67,0:14:47.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't tell you to stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.25,0:14:49.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You looked like \Nyou wanted to stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.81,0:15:00.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Colonel Mustang!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.85,0:15:03.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry to drop in on you \Nso unexpectedly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.29,0:15:05.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was just in the neighborhood.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.55,0:15:08.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, thank you for taking the trouble to see me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.25,0:15:11.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on, Elicia, \Ncan you say hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.01,0:15:13.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey there, Elicia. \NHow are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.77,0:15:20.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, come on inside. \NI'll serve some tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.11,0:15:29.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, I still have \Nsome work to attend to,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.69,0:15:30.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so I'll be leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.03,0:15:34.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Like I said...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.79,0:15:39.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's much more frightening to take on a live person.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.87,0:15:43.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Indeed, this is perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.26,0:15:45.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing in here about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.00,0:15:47.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There aren't any more documents that Hughes left behind, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.13,0:15:48.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, nothing more.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.63,0:15:50.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fine, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.35,0:15:52.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dispose of all of these materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.12,0:15:53.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't even leave ashes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.21,0:15:56.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But these are official \Nmilitary documents...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.49,0:15:57.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't care.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.48,0:16:02.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The 5th Laboratory \Nhad been shut down.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.29,0:16:04.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's only natural that there wouldn't be any records, wouldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.90,0:16:08.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there are {\i1}too{\i0} few of them. Even if it was shut down,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.02,0:16:10.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it's not natural for there not to be any records of installation maintenance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.90,0:16:12.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someone was \Nneglecting their duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.35,0:16:15.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean Brig. Gen. Grand?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.27,0:16:17.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you trying to say?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.01,0:16:20.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That it wasn't a mishap with the records, but that there {\i1}are{\i0} no records.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.49,0:16:23.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is evidence that there was \Na military directive to cover it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.21,0:16:28.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Though I couldn't imagine that the Führer was aware of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.34,0:16:31.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Chimeras that were \Nformed from humans...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.61,0:16:34.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Amplification of alchemic powers \Nby means of a Philosopher's Stone...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.92,0:16:37.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Both would be powerful military assets in battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.05,0:16:40.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You {\i1}do{\i0} know that those techniques are forbidden, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.16,0:16:43.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Science is the result \Nof trial and error.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.67,0:16:45.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Failing to utilize the mistakes of the past by learning from them,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.24,0:16:49.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and abandoning them as being too dangerous would be foolish, would it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.29,0:16:54.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, I have Zolf Kimbly and Shou Tucker under me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.20,0:16:55.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All I would need is your order.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.78,0:16:59.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a rebellion \Nstarting up again in Liore.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.45,0:17:02.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is also intelligence that Scar is in hiding.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.76,0:17:05.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How would you like to \Ntest your powers there?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.10,0:17:06.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.58,0:17:11.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For Pete's sake... For grown men to all gang up over some ghostly disturbance...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.59,0:17:13.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But we really are frightened.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.37,0:17:15.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, having you along will be a great help.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.14,0:17:17.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's just investigate this quick \Nand go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.14,0:17:21.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,From here on, the streetlights are out, so there's no light.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.89,0:17:24.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is Maintenance up to?! This is dereliction of duty!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.54,0:17:29.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That should do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.40,0:17:35.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's just your shadow, you idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.90,0:17:39.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant Fuery, if you do this, you can make shadows fun!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.48,0:17:41.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See? It's a cute doggie.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.62,0:17:43.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Woof! Woof!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.38,0:17:49.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop being so scared by everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.80,0:17:50.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's easy for you to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.83,0:17:52.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We really are scared!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.10,0:17:53.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I want to go home.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.10,0:17:55.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You call yourselves my men?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.43,0:17:57.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on! I'll prove to you that there are no ghosts!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.67,0:18:00.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't leave us behind, Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.80,0:18:03.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here is Warehouse 12.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.66,0:18:06.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Beyond it is just an empty lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.10,0:18:09.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look! Where do you \Nsee Warehouse 13?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.87,0:18:12.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Maybe it's hiding because \Nthere are a lot of people here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.09,0:18:13.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Enough already!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.39,0:18:16.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could it be that they mean {\i1}that{\i0} \Nwhen they say 13?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.83,0:18:23.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The letter "B" from the alphabet. It looked like the number 13.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.64,0:18:25.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's true, you could mistake it for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.80,0:18:28.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, in the dark and out of fear, what you did was misread it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.45,0:18:30.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez, you're such a scaremonger.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.88,0:18:33.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look! Once you realize what you're dealing with, that's all there is to it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.21,0:18:34.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what about the ghosts?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.80,0:18:36.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They don't exist!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.16,0:18:40.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank goodness! Now I can relax walking past here tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.25,0:18:41.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now that you know, \Nwe're done here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.63,0:18:42.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.39,0:18:45.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now that I can relax, \NI'm feeling hungry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.45,0:18:47.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Once we get back, \Nhow about some supper?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.01,0:18:48.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys are buying tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.39,0:18:50.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? I don't have any money!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.11,0:18:51.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's what you get \Nfor scaring us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.92,0:18:52.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.89,0:18:53.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.92,0:18:54.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.77,0:18:57.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.44,0:18:59.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Looks like something \Nwas dug up here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.14,0:19:00.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.06,0:19:00.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Falman!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.70,0:19:01.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.37,0:19:14.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.06,0:19:19.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A bone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.76,0:19:23.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sure enough, it's the ghost of an executed prisoner!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.63,0:19:25.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-It's really here!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.81,0:19:28.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Calm down! Even if this were an execution grounds,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.77,0:19:30.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they wouldn't be burying them here too, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.54,0:19:32.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a case of someone \Ndumping a body.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.54,0:19:36.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A body illegally dumped in a place \Nsaid to be a former execution grounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.03,0:19:40.53,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,There aren't any criminals who would come \Nall the way onto a military base just to bury this.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.53,0:19:44.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which means, you're saying that \Nthis is an incident internal to the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.07,0:19:48.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's highly possible. It's also possible that this bone belongs to a soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.54,0:20:05.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Establishing the identity of \Nthe victim is our top priority!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.44,0:20:06.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do not overlook anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.08,0:20:08.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They won't necessarily be buried in just one spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.85,0:20:10.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dig up anywhere \Nthat looks suspicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.64,0:20:11.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Roger!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:37.11,0:20:40.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, would you mind if I \Ntold you what I'm thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.22,0:20:47.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's the one who put us up to this nonsense?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.90,0:20:56.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Has something happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.30,0:20:57.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Never mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.94,0:21:08.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.04,0:21:12.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, the tiger is on the move.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.46,0:21:16.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm looking forward to \Nhearing good things from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.65,0:21:17.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Excuse me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.78,0:21:19.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.57,0:21:22.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I request permission to go along with the dispatch eastward.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.55,0:21:26.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have requested Major Armstrong to oversee combat on this trip.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.54,0:21:28.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Major is staying \Noff the front lines
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.55,0:21:30.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,due to the injuries he sustained in the recent fighting in Ishbal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.56,0:21:34.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I question whether the Major, who has not particularly distinguished himself in battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.04,0:21:36.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,should be given command of the forces on the front line.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.56,0:21:40.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I also have a responsibility to this case, \Nhaving once been stationed
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.41,0:21:42.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,at the Eastern Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.61,0:21:44.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please allow me to \Ngo along with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.32,0:21:48.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have no objections.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.32,0:21:51.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very well. \NColonel Roy Mustang,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.52,0:21:54.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I hereby order you to go along with \Nthe eastern suppression detachment.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.77,0:21:56.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I humbly accept your order!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.19,0:23:40.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.96,0:23:43.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 38: "With the River's Flow"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.88,0:23:46.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whenever I fought...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.41,0:23:48.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whenever I fought with Brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.03,0:23:51.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would always hunch down on the bank of the river.
